From 2d6cc352e45d73f6c61b71379c9ad13947f5a3e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adwait Nayak <quic_adwaitn@quicinc.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Mar 2025 02:29:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] QSDK:DP: wifi: ath12k: Enable various pktlog mode support

This change is responsible for enabling pktlog support in ath12k.

Change description:
1. User config portion to enable filter settings for different
   pktlog modes, is modified. Instead of numeric values, user
   needs to provide strings (filters and mode) as input.
   Old format:
   pktlog lite:
   echo "0x3 1" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter
   pktlog full (TX + RX):
   echo "0x3 2" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter
   Disabling pktlog filter:
   echo "0x0 0" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter

   New Format:
   In this design, we are supporting two modes and below filters:
   Mode: Lite, Full
   Filter: TX, RX, RCU, RCF
   It is recommended to use one mode at a time, along with
   one or multiple filters.
   pktlog lite: (Enables both tx and rx pktlog lite)
   echo "lite" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter
   pktlog lite tx/rx along with rate code debug:
   echo "lite,rcu,rcf" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter

   pktlog full: Both Tx and Rx full packet log is enabled with this
   change.
   Ex: pktlog full rx:
   echo "rx,full" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter

   Disabling/ resetting pktlog filter:
   echo "reset" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog_filter

   After configuring the mode and filter, invoke below commands to start
   packet log capture.
   echo 1 > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog/start
   to stop the capture:
   echo 0 > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/<hw>/macX/pktlog/start

2. HTT TLV filter settings for each pktlog mode is properly defined.
3. pktlog start and stop commands remain unchanged.
4. word mask subscription is disabled when pktlog is enabled.
5. Do not send WMI event to FW to enable pktlog, during filter
   or mode setting. Send it when pktlog start command is issued.
6. Enable global config bit and other params.
7. Pass actual buffer length instead of a fixed buffer length
   while sending pktlog buffer from dp_mon layer to pktlog
   buffer handler.

Signed-off-by: Adwait Nayak <quic_adwaitn@quicinc.com>
